# A stage0 sample from the audit: a division whose divisor reaches zero, which
# traps (exit code 70) in the built executable as under `refined run`.
divtrap is module
divtrap purpose "Divide by a number that reaches zero, so the program traps"
divtrap path divtrap
divtrap imports standard.console
divtrap imports standard.math
divtrap exports main

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter purpose "Authority to write lines to standard output"
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout none

main is operation
main purpose "Print 100 divided by 3, 2, 1, then trap dividing by 0"
main invariant none
main typeParameter none
main input none
main output ExitCode
main outputOwnedBy none
main raises none
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memoryHeap false
main async false
main maxRecursion none
main label begin loopKind none
main label begin within none
main label each loopKind while
main label each within none
main label each maxIterations limit
main label writeQDone loopKind none
main label writeQDone within each
main let d Int64 3 mutable
main let limit Int64 10 immutable
main let okCode ExitCode 0 immutable
main let hundred Int64 100 immutable
main let one Int64 1 immutable
main at begin goto each
main at each do divide
main at each do writeQ
main at each branch ifError writeQ goto writeQDone else goto writeQDone
main at writeQDone do lower
main at writeQDone set d nextD
main at writeQDone goto each

divide is call
divide in main
divide invokes math.divideInt64
divide argument left Int64 hundred copy
divide argument right Int64 d copy
divide result q Int64
divide ownedBy none
divide cleanedBy none
divide borrows none
divide catch none
divide suppresses none

writeQ is call
writeQ rationale "The failure has nowhere to be reported, so it is discarded"
writeQ in main
writeQ invokes console.writeIntegerLine
writeQ argument value Int64 q copy
writeQ result none
writeQ ownedBy none
writeQ cleanedBy none
writeQ borrows none
writeQ catch writeQError console.WriteError
writeQ suppresses console.WriteError.failed

lower is call
lower in main
lower invokes math.subtractInt64
lower argument left Int64 d copy
lower argument right Int64 one copy
lower result nextD Int64
lower ownedBy none
lower cleanedBy none
lower borrows none
lower catch none
lower suppresses none
